 {tab==='About & submission'&&<>{sectionTitle('TaxProof, in plain language.','A working review prototype built from the supplied case-study packet.')}<div className="card"><h2>The idea</h2><p>Tax software gives you an answer. TaxProof helps you prove it. Every number leads to its calculation and source. Reviewers record what they checked, resolve uncertainty, and approve a specific revision. Changes preserve the original and reopen approval.</p><div className="split"><div><h3>How to use it</h3>{['Open the Review queue and select the duplicate-interest issue.','Click an evidence reference to inspect the source page.','Open the related Schedule B line and record an adjustment with a reason.','Return to the issue and document the conclusion and evidence.','Switch to a reviewer to approve; make another change to see the approval become stale.','Use Filing & records to inspect blockers, timeline replay and exports.'].map((t,i)=><div className="issue" key={t}><span className="stepnum">{i+1}</span><p style={{margin:0}}>{t}</p></div>)}</div><div><h3>Technical decisions</h3><p>React and TypeScript run the interface. This GitHub Pages edition runs entirely in the browser. IndexedDB saves review records and attachments on this device. Transactional revision checks detect conflicts between tabs. The supplied fictional packet is bundled with the app.</p><h3>What is simulated</h3><p>Source documents are rendered from the packet's printed content. Filing, signatures and agency statuses are demonstrations. Custom tax impacts use the packet's rates and are estimates. Supplied scenario results are kept separate.</p><h3>AI disclosure</h3><p>AI assisted implementation and documentation. This app does not call an AI model at runtime. Checks, evidence lookup and approval gates are deterministic.</p></div></div><div className="actions"><Button onClick={()=>saveText('TaxProof-core-idea-and-data-model.md',onePager)}>Download one-page concept</Button><Button onClick={()=>saveText('TaxProof-error-findings.md',findings)}>Download findings report</Button><Button onClick={()=>saveText('TaxProof-video-walkthrough.md',videoScript)}>Download walkthrough script</Button></div></div><div className="card"><h2>Prototype boundaries</h2><p>Use this as a reviewable engineering demonstration, not production tax software. It does not transmit returns, execute legal e-signatures, rerun a tax engine, send external notifications, or automatically destroy records after seven years. Firm standards are scoped to this one engagement. An actual video of you explaining the app still needs to be recorded.</p></div></>}
